# Task B4.13: Command Code on Windows (F7), verified on the Windows VM (admin@192.168.65.3, Win11 ARM64,
# npm 11.19.0, node v24.20.0) on 2026-10-17 (VM local time 11:03-11:12 PDT, UTC 18:03-18:12).
#
# Build: harness v0.4.18-dev.c1afd3e39.dirty (HEAD c1afd3e39 plus this task's engineBin/launchSearchNames change and
# the driver's machine-id fix), the B4 install in C:\work\b4 (port 18475). harness-pty.exe reused from the VM's
# 2026-10-17 build (pty/ unchanged since 2026-10-16).
# Controller rulings (task-B4.13-carries.md):
# - Hooks stay OFF (DISABLE_HOOK_INSTALL=true): this run verifies the launch only. Hooks verified in B4.15.
# - No npm -g. Command Code installed with `npm i --prefix C:\work\b4\cc command-code@latest` (1.84.0). npm put a
#   prefix install's shims in C:\work\b4\cc\node_modules\.bin (cmd, cmdc, command-code, commandcode: .cmd/.ps1/sh),
#   so that folder went first on the B4 daemon's PATH, for this run only (C:\work\b4\env.cmd, restored afterwards).
# - COMMANDCODE_HOME redirected. Command Code 1.84.0 itself never reads COMMANDCODE_HOME: its dist/cli.mjs builds
#   every home path as `${HOME ?? USERPROFILE}/.commandcode/...`. So the run also set HOME, and the run's env.cmd
#   added:
#     set "PATH=C:\work\b4\cc\node_modules\.bin;%PATH%"
#     set HOME=C:\work\b4\homes\commandcode
#     set COMMANDCODE_HOME=C:\work\b4\homes\commandcode\.commandcode
# - Port 18473 (C:\work\e2e's daemon) was checked before start: nothing listened on 18473 or 18475.
# - %USERPROFILE%\.commandcode did not exist before the run (`if exist` -> NO_CCHOME).
# - Before this fix `where cmd command-code cmdc` on the VM answered C:\Windows\System32\cmd.exe first (F7).

