## 5. Cleanup
# agent_delete was refused while Command Code ran (the known F5 hold: no conversation identity with hooks off). Per the
# F5 workaround, a real Ctrl+C (PowerShell [char]3 through `e2e.mjs type`) ended Command Code in its pane. The rows
# (the commandcode row and the terminal row the pane became) were then stopped and purged with agent_purge
# inspect/delete, from a one-off C:\work\b4\purge.mjs (deleted afterwards). Then: C:\work\b4\stop.cmd, the run's
# env.cmd restored, and `rmdir /s /q` on C:\work\b4\cc, C:\work\b4\homes\commandcode (and the empty
# C:\work\b4\homes) and %USERPROFILE%\.commandcode (created by this run). The B4 pty host this run started (pid
# 11972, created 11:03:30, no children, no panes) outlived the daemon by design. It was ended after its identity was
# checked (pid, creation time, exe path, command line, no children), with Stop-Process on that one pid and no /T.
